Subject: [PATCH] provider: a Google account's saved plan follows its quota
 reading, so `magpie accounts`, the Accounts list and Routing's rows show it
 too (#5621)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On top of 0xTotoroX's fix for #5621, which has the quota reading name the
plan Code Assist reports now. That reaches `magpie quota` and the usage
cards, but `magpie accounts` (accountRows), the GUI's account list
(a.plan) and Routing's account rows and key/group account pickers
(Account.Plan, built from Login.Plan by googleProvider) all show the plan
saved at sign-in or import, so they kept the old name. A real case on
v0.1.3377: an Antigravity account imported on 10-20 as Google AI Pro,
whose loadCodeAssist now gives paid tier free-tier (Antigravity Starter
Quota) and whose fetchAvailableModels marks gemini-4-argon disabled, is
still listed as "· Google AI Pro" by `magpie accounts`.

googleLoginQuota now writes a plan that differs from the saved one to the
saved account (keepGooglePlan, as keepPluginPlan does for a plugin's
account). The quota keeps the saved plan when the reading fails or names
none, so those cases write nothing. A Gemini CLI login magpie keeps no
account of is left alone (editSideLogin finds none).

Verified: TestGoogleQuotaPlanFollowsCodeAssist now also checks
Logins(agent) after the reading. With the write-back gated off, it fails
the upgraded-to-Pro, upgraded-to-Ultra, downgraded and no-saved-plan
cases for both antigravity and gemini ("saved account after the
reading: … Plan:Antigravity Starter Quota …, want plan \"Google AI
Pro\""); no-plan-returned and failed-load pass either way, as they
should. On ce6ae593c with 0xTotoroX's commit cherry-picked first (clean),
go1.26.8, temp HOME with Go's caches pinned, on linux/amd64 (Ubuntu
24.04 VM), linux/arm64 (Debian container) and darwin/arm64: gofmt -l and
git diff --check are clean; go vet -tags nogui ./... and go build -tags
nogui ./... pass; go test -tags nogui ./... passes internal/provider,
internal/gateway and internal/gui on darwin. Every other failure in the
full runs also fails alone on clean ce6ae593c in the same environment
(running as root or in a container; among them internal/agent's TestAside*,
internal/proc's process-tree tests, internal/cli's TestKeyNote and
TestShareLines, internal/gui's TestBootSaysWhereItsGatewayListens,
internal/gateway's TestPrivateDialerRefusesPrivateAddresses; on this
Mac, internal/plugin's TestPluginSOCKSProxy). GUI suites not run: no GUI
code changed.
